cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FracFixD in your research, please cite both the software (Zenodo DOI below) and the FracFixR method paper (preferred-citation)."
title: "FracFixD: a native-D rewrite of FracFixR for fast compositional fractional fixup and differential proportion testing"
abstract: >
  FracFixD is a native-D, single-binary, GUI-and-CLI compositional
  statistics tool for fractionated RNA sequencing assays.  It
  re-implements the FracFixR method (non-negative least squares
  fraction recovery and beta-binomial differential proportion
  testing) in compiled native code for pipeline-scale throughput.
  Designed for polysome profiling, subcellular fractionation,
  monosome/disome profiling, and any other RNA-fractionation assay.
